  "description": "A self-addressing inception whose SAID and prefix carry the SHA2-256 code (I) while their value is the Blake3-256 digest of the body. The SAID verification protocol computes the digest with the algorithm the SAID's own code names (CESR line 1194), so the SAID does not verify and the inception must not be accepted. A validator that always uses Blake3, whatever the code says, accepts it. The case needs no digest feature, because a validator without SHA2-256 refuses it too.",
